See also:
    http://sb9.astro.ulb.ac.be : the SB9 home page
    V/64 : Eighth Orbital Elements of Spectroscopic Binaries (Batten+ 1989)

Byte-by-byte Description of file: main.dat
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Bytes Format Units   Label   Explanations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1-  4  I4    ---     Seq     System Number
                                (SB8 number when Seq<=1469)
   6- 15  A10   ---     B1900   Name based on B1900 position
                                (for backward compatibility with SB8=Cat. V/64)
  17- 18  I2    h       RAh     Right Ascension J2000 (hours)
  19- 20  I2    min     RAm     Right Ascension J2000 (minutes)
  21- 25  F5.2  s       RAs     Right Ascension J2000 (seconds)
      26  A1    ---     DE-     Declination J2000 (sign)
  27- 28  I2    deg     DEd     Declination J2000 (degrees)
  29- 30  I2    arcmin  DEm     Declination J2000 (minutes)
  31- 34  F4.1  arcsec  DEs     Declination J2000 (seconds)
  36- 42  A7    ---     Comp    ? Component
  44- 49  F6.3  mag     mag1    ? Magnitude of component 1
      50  A1    ---   n_mag1    [GJPBVRyrIK] Filter in which mag1 is given
  52- 57  F6.3  mag     mag2    ? Magnitude of component 2
      58  A1    ---   n_mag2    [PBVRyrIK] Filter in which mag2 is given
  60- 91  A32   ---     Sp1     MK Spectral type component 1
  93-102  A10   ---     Sp2     MK Spectral type component 2
 104-132  A29   ---     Name    Name of the source (HIP when existing)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Byte-by-byte Description of file: alias.dat
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Bytes Format Units   Label     Explanations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1-  4  I4    ---     Seq       System Number, as in "main.dat"
   6- 39  A34   ---     Name      Other designation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Byte-by-byte Description of file: orbits.dat
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Bytes Format Units   Label   Explanations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1-  4  I4    ---     Seq     System Number, as in "main.dat"
       6  I1    ---     o       Orbit number
   8- 23  F16.9 d       Per     [0.05,116675] Period
      25  A1    ---   f_Per     [a] a=assumed (fixed)
  26- 40  F15.9 d     e_Per     ? Mean error on Per
  42- 57  F16.8 d       T0      ? Periastron time (JD)
      59  A1    ---   n_T0      [a] a=assumed (fixed)
  60- 72  F13.8 d     e_T0      ? Mean error on T0
  74- 77  F4.1  ---   f_T0      ? Flag on T0 (2)
  79- 89  F11.9 ---     e       Orbital eccentricity
      91  A1    ---   f_e       [>a] a=assumed (fixed) (1)
  92-102  F11.9 ---   e_e       ? Mean error on eccentricity
 104-112  F9.4  deg     omega   [-359,360]? Argument of periastron {omega}
     114  A1    ---   f_omega   [a] a=assumed (fixed)
 115-122  F8.4  deg   e_omega   ? Mean error on omega
 124-133  F10.5 km/s    K1      ? Velocity amplitude of primary
     134  A1    ---   u_K1      Uncertainty flag (:) on K1
     136  A1    ---   f_K1      [>a] a=assumed (fixed) (1)
 137-146  F10.5 km/s  e_K1      ?   Mean error on K1
 148-157  E10.5 km/s    K2      ? Velocity amplitude of secondary
     158  A1    ---   u_K2      Uncertainty flag (:) on K2
     160  A1    ---   f_K2      [a] a=assumed (fixed)
 161-170  E10.5 km/s  e_K2      ?  Mean error on K2
 172-181  E10.5 km/s    V0      ? Systemtic velocity
     182  A1    ---   u_V0      Uncertainty flag (:) on V0
     184  A1    ---   f_V0      [a] a=assumed (fixed)
 185-194  F10.5 km/s  e_V0      ?  Mean error on V0
 196-204  F9.6  km/s    rms1    ? rms residuals of Radial Velocity primary
 206-214  F9.6  km/s    rms2    ? rms residuals of Radial Velocity secondary
 216-219  I4    ---   o_K1      ? Number of observations of RV1
 221-224  I4    ---   o_K2      ? Number of observations of RV2
 226-228  F3.1  ---     Grade   ? Grade of orbit (0=poor, 5=definitive)
 230-280  A51   ---     Ref     Reference (bibcode) of orbit publication
 282-291  A10   ---     Contr   Contributor
 293-295  A3    ---     ---     [PUB] Access code (public)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note (1): the symbol '>' indicates that the error is large
     (larger than the value); the symbol 'a' indicates that the
     value was not computed, but assumed.
Note (2): a non-zero value indicates that T0 does not correspond to the
     periastron epoch, but to some other phenomena (e.g. eclipse)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

